      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "Rest and spread are important syntax to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "Now I want to dive into another important feature and that is the structuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "Now let me comment out this code down there and let's begin with Object D structuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 25.68,
          "en": "I got my personal object and now let's say we have some code where I only need to name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 26.19,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "So I have a new function print name, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "And that actually takes the full person object because for whatever reason we write wrote it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 45.99,
          "en": "or we simply have a function where we are able to get multiple arguments or a full object because some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 45.99,
          "end": 48.48,
          "en": "third party package always gives us that person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 48.48,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "We can't change that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 55.89,
          "en": "So we get the person here and I only want to console.log person that name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 60.37,
          "end": 62.8,
          "en": "Now that is totally fine of doing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 63.04,
          "end": 65.74,
          "en": "I can now execute a print name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 65.77,
          "end": 70.39,
          "en": "Now I need to pass person here now to avoid naming confusion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 70.39,
          "end": 71.05,
          "en": "Confusion?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 71.05,
          "end": 73.27,
          "en": "You can name this here however you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 73.27,
          "end": 76.06,
          "en": "So here we could name it person data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 76.06,
          "end": 77.95,
          "en": "And inside here we use person data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 77.95,
          "end": 80.47,
          "en": "So that function does not use that person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 80.47,
          "end": 82.51,
          "en": "It just expects any person data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 82.51,
          "end": 86.56,
          "en": "We then call that function and pass in that person as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 86.98,
          "end": 91.75,
          "en": "And now if they execute that file, I see Max here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.93,
          "end": 94.45,
          "en": "This is stemming from this line here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 94.81,
          "end": 97.27000000000001,
          "en": "Now, of course, we can absolutely do it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 97.69,
          "end": 103.09,
          "en": "And we always get person data because again, let's say this is a function which is actually called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 103.09,
          "end": 107.14,
          "en": "by some third party package, which is a pattern you see quite a bit throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 107.95,
          "end": 114.75999999999999,
          "en": "Now, therefore, we can't change the data we get, but in this function here we are only interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 114.75999999999999,
          "end": 115.81,
          "en": "in the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 116.17,
          "end": 123.34,
          "en": "We can then use a syntax or a feature called Object D structuring where we add curly braces here in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 123.34,
          "end": 123.88,
          "en": "the.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 124.9,
          "end": 129.19,
          "en": "Argument list and we then specify the property of the incoming object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 129.19,
          "end": 131.32,
          "en": "We are interested in name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 131.47,
          "end": 134.26,
          "en": "That is this property we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 134.95,
          "end": 138.97,
          "en": "Then this will be pulled out of the incoming object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 138.97,
          "end": 145.6,
          "en": "The other properties will be dropped for this function and it will be stored in a variable named name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 145.6,
          "end": 147.22,
          "en": "which we then can use in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 147.49,
          "end": 149.44,
          "en": "So now if I execute this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 151.76,
          "end": 157.85,
          "en": "I also see Max, but now we're using this de structuring syntax and we can pull out the FF too if you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 157.85,
          "end": 158.57,
          "en": "want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 158.81,
          "end": 160.46,
          "en": "Or the grid function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 160.82,
          "end": 162.26,
          "en": "So that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 162.26,
          "end": 170.03,
          "en": "And that is just a syntax we can use that allows us to write a bit of a more understandable code where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 170.03,
          "end": 175.49,
          "en": "we are very clear about what we need from the incoming object and which then gets stored in a local",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 175.49,
          "end": 178.52,
          "en": "variable that we can just use in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 178.7,
          "end": 183.44,
          "en": "And you can of course not just use the structuring inside of a function, you can always use it outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 183.44,
          "end": 183.92,
          "en": "of there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 183.92,
          "end": 191.66,
          "en": "You can create a new constant here, for example, and then the syntax will look like this curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 191.69,
          "end": 196.22,
          "en": "equals person, curly braces on the left side of the equals sign or something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 196.22,
          "end": 201.11,
          "en": "We don't see that often in JavaScript because typically it's wrong, but for the structuring it's correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 201.26,
          "end": 207.89,
          "en": "And then here we can have the name and the H and this will create two new constants which hold the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 207.89,
          "end": 209.21,
          "en": "stored in name and H.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 209.21,
          "end": 217.91,
          "en": "So these names here have to match the property names of the person and now we can console, log name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 217.91,
          "end": 219.47,
          "en": "and h like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 219.74,
          "end": 221.9,
          "en": "If I now re executed file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 221.93,
          "end": 228.8,
          "en": "This output here is coming from this console log and the values we're outputting here are retrieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 228.8,
          "end": 231.41,
          "en": "via object D structuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 233.88,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "Now, there's also not just object restructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 239.4,
          "en": "You can also restructure, erase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 241.53,
          "en": "So if we go back to the hobbies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 243.27,
          "en": "What you have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 244,
          "end": 246.61,
          "en": "Well, then, if we would want to structure that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 247.81,
          "end": 250.49,
          "en": "We can also create a cost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 250.51,
          "end": 253.78,
          "en": "You could also use led, by the way, the same for the object restructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 253.78,
          "end": 263.65,
          "en": "If you plan on changing it, you could use a cost for hobby one and hobby two wrapped in square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 268.17,
          "en": "And then assign this to hobbies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "And now if you console.log hobby one and you console log hobby two and you execute that file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 280.03,
          "en": "you see the two hobbies being printed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 280.05,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "Please note there are no square brackets around them in the console log because we're not logging in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 286.83,
          "en": "array here we are logging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 286.83,
          "end": 290.15999999999997,
          "en": "Q Individual values, which we got via.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 291.35,
          "end": 293.06,
          "en": "Air raid restructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 294.23,
          "end": 301.34,
          "en": "Unlike the object restructuring here, you can choose any names you want because in a race your elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 301.34,
          "end": 302.51,
          "en": "have no names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 302.51,
          "end": 305.42,
          "en": "They are instead pulled out by position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 305.42,
          "end": 307.64,
          "en": "So this will always be the first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 307.64,
          "end": 310.64,
          "en": "This will be the second element in objects.",
